id: spiked
name: Spiked
kind: crafting
categories: armor
slots: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Struck by an Unarmed Physical Attack from beside you, they lose the Apparel Bonus in Life
  Points.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Automatic]: When you are struck by an Unarmed Physical Attack from an Opponent on an adjacent
  Square to you, reduce their Life Points by the Apparel Bonus for this piece of Armor.
text: >
  Spiked: This armor is covered in sharpened spikes to retaliate against anyone who tries to
  strike you.
  –Apparel Category: Armor
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: When you are struck by an Unarmed Physical Attack from an Opponent on an adjacent
  Square to you, reduce their Life Points by the Apparel Bonus for this piece of Armor.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Physical Attack that hits whoever is wearing it - dealing Damage or not - posts a card: the
# one who struck, and this piece's Apparel Bonus at the wearer's base Tier. Its button, for the
# GM and whoever plays the wearer, takes that many Life Points off the one who struck: a Life
# Point reduction, past Soak and Damage Reduction. Dense Armor on the piece raises what it takes.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The adjacent Square, and that they are an Opponent: the button is pressed only when they were.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Unarmed": there are no Weapons in this system yet, so every Physical Attack is Unarmed. When
# they arrive, one made with a Weapon posts no card.

[passive]
piece.spikes = true;
